                        kind @note
                        text "Split out of errors-idiomatic.parser after sizing. The blast-radius survey recorded the applicator side of the ParseTagState conversion as \"one function — GrammarApplicator::add_tag\". That function has 81 call sites across 18 files: apertium_applicator 15, run_grammar 11, core 9, jsonl 8, matxin 7, plaintext 6, fst 4, niceline 3, grammar 3, reflow 2, and singletons elsewhere, plus 8 in tests. Folding that into the parser node would have made an already-atomic 30-signature conversion span another 81 sites in code that has nothing to do with parsing. Kept separate so the parser conversion stays reviewable. Until this lands, Matcher::add_tag absorbs the ParseError from parse_tag rather than propagating it — which still removes the inherited UB panic characterised in tests/applicator_tag_fallthrough.rs, because the error is handled instead of execution continuing into is_textual with empty text."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-14T16:21:03.598954Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
