                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-15T14:49:07.965495Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "tools/vislcg3.rs:60 compiles the --nrules / --nrules-inv patterns with a bare regex::Regex::new, bypassing crate::tag_regex::compile_tag_regex. [spec:cg3:req:tag-regex.single-seam] says every tag pattern goes through the seam; a rule-name filter is not strictly a tag pattern, which is why this was left alone, but it is user-authored and the C++ compiled it with the same ICU engine as everything else. So an ICU-spelled --nrules pattern silently gets different semantics from the identical pattern in a grammar: no \\Q...\\E, no ICU \\Z or $, and possessive quantifiers mis-parsed rather than rejected. Either route it through the seam or state in the spec why a filter is exempt."
                    }

